{"name":"Seine and Sensibility","hex":"#ccc4b0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"seine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long net having floats attached at the top and sinkers (weights) at the bottom, used in shallow water for catching fish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To use a seine, to fish with a seine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seine"},{"term":"and","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Ansus."]},{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["As a coordinating conjunction; expressing two elements to be taken together or in addition to each other.\nUsed simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n\nSimply connecting two clauses or sentences. \n\nIntroducing a clause or sentence which follows on in time or consequence from the first.","Used simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/and"},{"term":"sensibility","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Emotions or feelings arising from or relating to aesthetic or moral standards, especially those which are sensitive and thus likely to be hurt or offended. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The ability to feel, perceive, or sense; responsiveness to sensory stimuli; sensitivity; also, the degree to which someone or something (especially a sensory organ or tissue) is able to respond to sensory stimuli."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sensibility"}],"entries":[{"title":"Seine","blocks":[{"text":"The Seine is a 777-kilometre-long (483 mi) river in northern France. Its drainage basin is in the Paris Basin covering most of northern France. It rises at Source-Seine, 30 kilometres (19 mi) northwest of Dijon in northeastern France in the Langres plateau, flowing through Paris and into the English Channel at Le Havre. It is navigable by ocean-going vessels as far as Rouen, 120 kilometres (75 mi) from the sea. Over 60 percent of its length, as far as Burgundy, is negotiable by large barges and most tour boats, and nearly its whole length is available for recreational boating; excursion boats offer sightseeing tours of the river banks in the capital city, Paris."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Bercy%2C_Paris_01.jpg/330px-Bercy%2C_Paris_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seine","wikidata":"Q1471"},{"title":"Sensibility","blocks":[{"text":"Sensibility refers to an acute perception of or responsiveness toward something, such as the emotions of another. This concept emerged in eighteenth-century Britain, and was closely associated with studies of sense perception as the means through which knowledge is gathered. It also became associated with sentimental moral philosophy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Emma_Hamilton...Stipple_engraving%2C_1789._Wellcome_L0075392.jpg/330px-Emma_Hamilton...Stipple_engraving%2C_1789._Wellcome_L0075392.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sensibility","wikidata":"Q1195509"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Bassin_Seine.png/500px-Bassin_Seine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Bassin_Seine.png/1280px-Bassin_Seine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Bassin_Seine.png/500px-Bassin_Seine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABassin_Seine.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/